Z||000003||Raydar||08-30-2001||10:17 AM||||Umm.... I'm guessing a 3.1 crank?<BR>A 3.4 is a bored out 3.1. Same crank, if I'm not mistaken.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||08-30-2001||11:47 AM||||A 3.1 is a 2.8 block with a longer stroke crank.<P>A 3.4 is a beefier block than the 2.8/3.1, but shares the same crank as the 3.1.<P>You cannot bore out a 2.8/3.1 big enough to equal the displacement of a 3.4 without some real problems (cyl. walls are too thin).<P>A 3.4 is actually a 3.35, but that's another story.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  ||||reg||1
